From 13e5878d648d835e4af3910b6e94fef30794f1b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Pitt <martin@piware.de>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:17:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pcap: Declare the USB pseudo-header layout ourselves

libpcap 1.11 changed the 64 bit members of pcap_usb_header_mmapped into a
pair of 32 bit halves, which breaks our binding that reads them as uint64.
No distribution ships 1.11 yet, so we have to keep building against both.

DLT_USB_LINUX_MMAPPED is a frozen on-disk format, so declare it ourselves
instead of binding libpcap's struct. Static assertions check our definition
against whichever libpcap we are built against, so a layout mistake fails
the build instead of silently corrupting a replay. It has to live in a C
header rather than in Vala code, as valac warns about the members we never
read, which is fatal with --werror.

This also fixes what made libpcap change the header in the first place:
pcap_next() only guarantees 4 byte alignment for the records it hands out,
so reading them through a struct that wants 8 byte alignment is undefined
behaviour on architectures which care.

Fixes #284
---
 meson.build            |  2 +
 src/libpcap.vapi       | 29 -------------
 src/pcap_usb.h         | 93 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/pcap_usb.vapi      | 38 +++++++++++++++++
 src/umockdev-pcap.vala | 24 +++++------
 5 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/pcap_usb.h
 create mode 100644 src/pcap_usb.vapi

